BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Requiem For A King – Music of Jean Gilles and Marc-Antoine Charp
 entier
DTSTART:20261030T193000
DTEND:20261030T220000
DTSTAMP:20261030T170326Z
UID:deafe9d08a48ee5e78d011d3ed2a22@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Burlington Baroque presents the rediscovered Funeral Requiem S
 etting of Jean Gilles (1668 - 1705) featuring internationally acclaimed fe
 stival Artists-in-Residence L’Harmonie des saisons Baroque Orchestra and
  the Burlington Baroque Festival Singers\, directed by Eric Milnes. Jean G
 illes’ Messe des Morts\, the most frequently performed Requiem in 18th-c
 entury France\, will receive its regional premiere in two upcoming perform
 ances: Friday\, October 30\, at 7:30 p.m. at Holy Angels Church in St. Alb
 ans\, and Sunday\, November 1\, at 4:00 p.m. at College Street Congregatio
 nal Church in Burlington. Forgotten for more than a century and a half\, G
 illes reemerged from obscurity in the 1950s\, largely through the rediscov
 ery of this Funeral Mass. Born in Tarascon on January 8\, 1668\, he began 
 his musical life at the Cathedral of Saint-Sauveur in Aix-en-Provence as a
 ssistant to director of music Guillaume Poitevin\, whom he later succeeded
 . In 1697\, Gilles settled in Toulouse\, serving as director of music at t
 he Cathedral of Saint-Étienne until his death on February 5\, 1705\, at a
 ge 37. Although his career was brief and devoted entirely to sacred music
 \, his works were celebrated throughout the 18th century. The date and cir
 cumstances of the Requiem’s composition are unknown\, but the work becam
 e one of the 18th century’s most frequently performed pieces of sacred m
 usic and secured Gilles’ posthumous fame. A commentator wrote in 1756 th
 at “of all the Requiem masses\, the one written by Gilles has always bee
 n looked upon as the best.” The work was performed at official funeral o
 bservances\, including memorial services for Jean-Philippe Rameau in 1764 
 and Louis XV in 1774\, and entered the repertoire of the Concert Spirituel
  in 1750. Audiences should not miss this rare opportunity to experience th
 e timeless grandeur of this glorious masterpiece in live performance. Adul
 ts $40-$80\, $10 Student\, Children free\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Holy Angels Church\, 245 Lake St.
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/requiem-fo
 r-a-king-music-of-jean-gilles-and-marc-antoine-charpentier-04-10-2026-00-3
 5-57
END:VEVENT
